From 57f5c23228bac271abab4238f786a21b77c6b181 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 19:43:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6 Path B: switch wb_altremote_update wrapper to
 altremote_update IP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace direct cycloneive_rublock primitive instantiation + 29-bit shift
FSM with a thin wrapper around the altremote_update megafunction.  The
prior "Lite 21.1 strips write_param/data_in for Cyclone IV E REMOTE"
memory was REFUTED on 2026-05-20: quartus_map elaborates the IP via the
Verilog-instantiation + clearbox path and produces a fully-functional
auto_generated rmtupdt_ik21 with field decoders, rublock_clock divider,
and the proper write_param/data_in/reconfig protocol.

Switch rationale: 5 sessions of direct-primitive layout/timing debugging
exhausted.  4 layout hypotheses tested via mode X parametric reconfig on
2026-05-20, all caused fall-back to RoT.  The megafunction handles
field encoding + primitive clocking internally, eliminating the entire
class of layout/timing bugs.

RTL (rtl/wb_altremote_update.v): rewrote ~370 lines → ~170 lines.  New
register map:
  0x00 DATA   (R/W) data_in[23:0] write / data_out[28:0] read
  0x04 CTRL   (W)   [2:0]=param, [3]=write_param pulse, [4]=read_param,
                     [5]=reset_timer, [6]=reconfig, [9:8]=read_source
  0x08 STATUS (R)   [0]=busy

Firmware (sw/stage2_loader/remote_update.c): epcs_remote_reconfig_ex
now sequences 3 write_param calls (PAGE_SELECT=byte_addr, WD_ENABLE=0,
CD_EARLY=1) then triggers reconfig.  AnF is implicit in Cyclone IV
(pgm_sel != 0 means application, pgm_sel == 0 means factory) so the
ap_config_sel parameter is now ignored.

mode X (param reconfig) + mode Q (reconfig source read) updated to use
the new param protocol.

Iron status (2026-05-20 evening): bitstream md5 bb39b0b09f4f83d8...,
LE 8729/10320 (85%), flashed to EPCS page 0, mode X with byte_addr=
0x080000 fires reconfig but chip returns reconfig source = 4 (nSTATUS
asserted) = configuration error during slot-1 load.  TPU.rbf at slot 1
verified byte-identical to neorv32_tpu output AND SRAM-loadable via
openFPGALoader -m (so image is intrinsically valid).  Root cause now
narrowed to EPCS multi-image layout — slot 1 raw .rbf is missing the
metadata Quartus would normally inject via multi-page POF generation.
quartus_cpf -c multi-image .cof fails with "Illegal Configuration
Scheme does not support dual boot" in 21.1 Lite — needs more research.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
